From: Enable V4L2 video encoder on non-ChromeOS Linux
Subject: Remove IS_CHROMEOS guard from V4L2 encoder factory and BUILD.gn

Chromium gates the V4L2 video encode accelerator behind IS_CHROMEOS in
two places:
1. gpu_video_encode_accelerator_factory.cc — CreateV4L2VEA() returns
   nullptr on non-ChromeOS
2. media/gpu/v4l2/BUILD.gn — encoder source files only compiled for
   is_chromeos

This prevents the encoder from being instantiated and its supported
codec profiles from appearing in chrome://gpu on embedded Linux systems
with V4L2 encode hardware (e.g. Hantro H1 on NXP i.MX8MM).

Remove both IS_CHROMEOS conditionals so the V4L2 encoder is built and
created on all USE_V4L2_CODEC platforms.

Tested on: NXP i.MX8MM EVK with Chromium 129.0.6668.100
(Hantro H1 V4L2 encoder)

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [embedded platform enablement]

---

--- a/media/gpu/gpu_video_encode_accelerator_factory.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/gpu_video_encode_accelerator_factory.cc
@@ -47,14 +47,8 @@
 namespace {
 #if BUILDFLAG(USE_V4L2_CODEC)
 std::unique_ptr<VideoEncodeAccelerator> CreateV4L2VEA() {
-#if BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
-  // TODO(crbug.com/901264): Encoders use hack for passing offset within
-  // a DMA-buf, which is not supported upstream.
   return base::WrapUnique<VideoEncodeAccelerator>(
       new V4L2VideoEncodeAccelerator(new V4L2Device()));
-#else
-  return nullptr;
-#endif
 }
 #elif BUILDFLAG(USE_VAAPI)
 std::unique_ptr<VideoEncodeAccelerator> CreateVaapiVEA() {

--- a/media/gpu/v4l2/BUILD.gn
+++ b/media/gpu/v4l2/BUILD.gn
@@ -80,14 +80,15 @@
       # AV1 delegate depends on header files only in ChromeOS SDK
       "v4l2_video_decoder_delegate_av1.cc",
       "v4l2_video_decoder_delegate_av1.h",
-
-      # TODO(crbug.com/901264): Encoders use hack for passing offset
-      # within a DMA-buf, which is not supported upstream.
-      "v4l2_video_encode_accelerator.cc",
-      "v4l2_video_encode_accelerator.h",
     ]
   }

+  # V4L2 encoder — needed on any platform with V4L2 encode hardware
+  sources += [
+    "v4l2_video_encode_accelerator.cc",
+    "v4l2_video_encode_accelerator.h",
+  ]
+
   libs = [
     "EGL",
     "GLESv2",
